<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Mid-ordinate rule for a curve</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Use the mid-ordinate rule with \({@n@}\) strips to estimate the area bounded by \(y = {@fx@}\), the \(x\)-axis and the lines \(x = {@a@}\) and \(x = {@exd(b)@}\). Give exact values.</p><p>(a) What is the strip width \(h\)?</p><div>\(h =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) At what value of \(x\) is the first mid-ordinate?</p><div>\(x =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the mid-ordinate estimate of the area.</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) \(h = \dfrac{ {@exd(b)@} - {@a@} }{ {@n@} } = {@exd(hh)@}\).</p><p>(b) The height at the middle of a strip stands for the whole strip. The first strip runs from \(x = {@a@}\) to \(x = {@exd(a+hh)@}\), so its middle is at \(x = {@a@} + \tfrac{1}{2} \times {@exd(hh)@} = {@exd(x1)@}\).</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Middle \(x\)</th>[[foreach u="mids"]]<td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@exd(u)@}\)</td>[[/foreach]]</tr><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Mid-ordinate \(m\)</th>[[foreach u="ms"]]<td style="padding:4px 10px;">\({@exd(u)@}\)</td>[[/foreach]]</tr></table><p>(c) \(M = h(m_1 + \cdots + m_{ {@n@} }) = {@exd(hh)@} \times {@exd(apply("+",ms))@} = {@exd(Ma)@}\).</p><p>For comparison, the trapezoidal rule with the same strips gives \({@exd(Mt)@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* exd: shortest exact decimal display of a terminating value (up to 3 d.p.) */
exd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else if integerp(10*v) then dispdp(float(v),1) else if integerp(100*v) then dispdp(float(v),2) else dispdp(float(v),3);
/* Design: mid-ordinate rule: strip width, mid-ordinate positions, then the estimate; polynomial curves, exact values. Entries [a, h, n, c0, c1, c2]. a is never 0 and h/2 is never a, so h and the first mid-ordinate always differ; h is never 1 or 2. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 3, Chapter 9, Example 6. */
L: [[1,1/2,4,3,2,3],[2,3,4,100,0,-1/2],[1,4,3,20,2,-1/4],[3,1/2,4,1,2,4],[3,4,4,95,0,-1/4],[1,3,3,4,0,1/2],[4,1/2,4,52,-2,-1],[3,4,4,5,2,1/4],[3,3,4,150,-2,-1/2],[1,1/2,3,24,2,-4]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
a: L[ix][1]; hh: L[ix][2]; n: L[ix][3]; c0: L[ix][4]; c1: L[ix][5]; c2: L[ix][6];
b: a+n*hh;
f(t) := c0+c1*t+c2*t^2;
fx: c0+c1*x+c2*x^2;
mids: makelist(a+(j-1/2)*hh,j,1,n);
ms: map(f,mids);
Ma: hh*apply("+",ms);
x1: a+hh/2;
/* diagnostics */
edges: makelist(f(a+j*hh),j,0,n);
Ml: hh*apply("+",rest(edges,-1));
Mr: hh*apply("+",rest(edges));
Mt: hh/2*(first(edges)+last(edges)+2*apply("+",rest(rest(edges),-1)));
Mhalf: hh/2*apply("+",ms);
Mnoh: apply("+",ms);]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
