  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Area Approximations: mid-ordinate rule for a curve</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.2 (c) / Essential 2.1 (c): Find the strip width and the position of the first mid-ordinate, and estimate the area under a quadratic curve with the mid-ordinate rule.</p><p id="edition">Core and Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Example 6 in Section C of Chapter 9 of Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 3 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2005: strip width, mid-ordinate positions and the estimate, for polynomial curves with exact values and new intervals.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core and Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
